      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village began in 1844 when Cornelius Bogan opened a general store that became the town’s first commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.isabellatwp.com/about/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers called the spot Halfway because it lay roughly between Clare and Mount Pleasant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosebush%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The post office switched names several times—Rosebush in 1889, Calkinsville in 1890, and back to Rosebush in 1903.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosebush%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rosebush sits entirely within the Isabella Indian Reservation, home to the federally recognized Saginaw Chippewa Tribal Nation.",
